message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "zzrctsim: Simulation of Longitudinal Randomized Trials with Conditional and Marginal Data-Generating Mechanisms"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-14"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/rgt47/zzrctsim"
authors:
  - family-names: Thomas
    given-names: "Ronald G."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1686-4965"
    email: rgthomas@ucsd.edu
    affiliation: "Herbert Wertheim School of Public Health and Human Longevity Science, University of California San Diego"
abstract: >
  Simulates longitudinal randomized clinical trials in order to evaluate
  design and analysis choices. A data-generating mechanism for a continuous
  Gaussian outcome may be declared either conditionally, through random
  effects, or marginally, through a covariance matrix or a covariance
  function of time, with exact conversion between the two parameterizations
  where one exists and a computable rank certificate where it does not.
  Missingness follows the Diggle and Kenward (1994) selection model,
  calibrated to a target dropout proportion. Simulations follow Morris,
  White and Crowther (2019), with L'Ecuyer-CMRG substreams, per-replicate
  state capture, and performance measures reported with Monte Carlo
  standard errors.
keywords:
  - clinical-trials
  - simulation
  - longitudinal-data
  - statistical-power
  - missing-data
